Overlay patch 0037: VR camera unification (VR-spec D5, VR-DONOR-MAP §5).
Two halves at the tail of Camera_Update, and the ORDER between them is the
whole point.

(a) EXPORT the game camera's own eye + forward BEFORE anything VR touches the
    view. The shell seats VR's A matrix on this pair, never on play->view.eye
    -- which half (b) is about to overwrite. Anchoring VR on the view would
    chase our own HMD offset in a feedback loop; the donor records exactly
    that trap in its third-person block ("anchor from the camera's own eye,
    not play->view.eye", z_play.c:1483-1499). 0032's gSoh3DCam* export is
    taken inside z_view.c AFTER func_800AA358 and is therefore the polluted
    one -- it stays correct for the 3D panel (no VR write) and unusable as a
    VR anchor, which is why VR gets its own export here.

(b) In VR, replace the view's eye/at/up/fov with the shell's composed head
    pose (donor's 32-line Camera_Update push, z_camera.c:7731-7761). Rendering
    is unaffected -- the interpreter builds clip space from the per-eye A.V.P
    that 0031 substitutes -- so the game View is used purely CPU-side: frustum
    culling, actor->projectedPos (audio panning) and LOD. Without this the
    game culls and draws its skybox from the GAME camera while the player
    looks from somewhere else, and everything outside the game frustum turns
    black the moment the head moves (VR-R0-FINDINGS finding 7, artifact 10).
    That is why spec D5 was promoted from "early and cheap" to BLOCKING for
    the first head-tracked frame.

Culling FOV comes from the shell already padded (donor VR_GetCullingFovy
shape: widest eye's vertical FOV x1.3, clamped to 90..160 deg) -- erring wide
costs a little geometry, erring narrow reintroduces edge pop-in. View scale is
forced back to 1.0 because the Hyrule Field 0.79 zoom just above would crop
the padded frustum again.

camDir/inputDir are deliberately NOT touched: they are computed from
eyeAtAngle further up, off the game camera's own eye/at, so third-person stick
steering stays camera-relative exactly as in flat play (donor's own note).

rev2 (VR R2b): the active camera's `setting` is exported too, purely as a
diagnostic -- `vr room` needs it to say whether an image-backed room is being
drawn under CAM_SET_PREREND_FIXED (background drawn) or under something else
(bare placeholder geometry, the green floor).

rev3 (VR R3) -- THE GREEN FLOOR, ESTABLISHED RATHER THAN INFERRED. R2b blamed
the DisableFixedCamera enhancement for Link's house showing a bare, untextured
green floor on the panel, and forced that enhancement off in room mode 0. That
was inference, and it was at best incomplete: the actual mechanism is HERE.

Half (b) overwrote the game View with the HEAD POSE whenever gSohVRMode != 0 --
including in a FLAT-SCREEN context. A pre-rendered room (Link's house, the
shops, Kakariko interiors) is presented on the world-locked panel precisely so
its authored 2D art reads correctly, and that art was authored FOR THE FIXED
CAMERA. Driving the View from the head there means the frame the panel shows is
no longer the frame the artwork belongs to: the background image and the room
geometry disagree, and what survives is the placeholder mesh -- whose floor in
Link's house is an untextured green quad.

Camera unification exists to stop geometry popping as you turn your head in an
immersive frame. A flat context has no immersive frame; the panel IS the game
camera's own picture. So rev3 gates half (b) on gSohVRFlatLatch == 0, the same
tick-boundary latch overlays 0039/0041/0043 use, and the panel gets the game
camera's frame byte for byte. Half (a), the basis export, is unconditional as
before -- it is a read.

__IOS__-only; the macOS build and the iPhone build compile the export half
with gSohVRMode permanently 0, so half (b) never fires there.

--- a/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/z_camera.c
@@ -7721,7 +7721,63 @@
         View_SetScale(&camera->play->view, 0.79f);
     } else {
         View_SetScale(&camera->play->view, 1.0f);
+    }
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    /* SOH_IOS (overlay 0037, VR-spec D5 / VR-DONOR-MAP 5): camera
+     * unification. (a) export the GAME camera's basis for VR's A matrix
+     * BEFORE (b) overwrites the view with the head pose -- anchoring VR on
+     * the view it just wrote is a feedback loop. See the patch header. */
+    {
+        extern volatile int gSohVRMode;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRFlatLatch;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRCamValid;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRAnchorValid;
+        extern volatile float gSohVRAnchorEye[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRAnchorFwd[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRCamEye[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRCamFwd[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRCamUp[3];
+        extern volatile float gSohVRCamFovy;
+        extern volatile int gSohVRCamSetting;
+        /* rev2 (VR R2b): the active camera's SETTING, for diagnostics. z_room.c
+         * draws a pre-rendered background only when this is CAM_SET_PREREND_FIXED
+         * (func_80096680), so `vr room` reading anything else in an image-backed
+         * room is the whole explanation for a bare, green-floored placeholder
+         * mesh on the panel. One store per Camera_Update, no behaviour. */
+        gSohVRCamSetting = (int)camera->setting;
+        float sohVRdx = viewAt.x - viewEye.x;
+        float sohVRdy = viewAt.y - viewEye.y;
+        float sohVRdz = viewAt.z - viewEye.z;
+        float sohVRlen = sqrtf(sohVRdx * sohVRdx + sohVRdy * sohVRdy + sohVRdz * sohVRdz);
+        if (sohVRlen > 0.001f) {
+            gSohVRAnchorEye[0] = viewEye.x;
+            gSohVRAnchorEye[1] = viewEye.y;
+            gSohVRAnchorEye[2] = viewEye.z;
+            gSohVRAnchorFwd[0] = sohVRdx / sohVRlen;
+            gSohVRAnchorFwd[1] = sohVRdy / sohVRlen;
+            gSohVRAnchorFwd[2] = sohVRdz / sohVRlen;
+            gSohVRAnchorValid = 1;
+        }
+        /* rev3 (VR R3): NEVER in a flat-screen context -- the panel must show
+         * the GAME camera's own frame, which is what the pre-rendered art was
+         * authored for. See the patch header. */
+        if ((gSohVRMode != 0) && (gSohVRCamValid != 0) && (gSohVRFlatLatch == 0)) {
+            viewEye.x = gSohVRCamEye[0];
+            viewEye.y = gSohVRCamEye[1];
+            viewEye.z = gSohVRCamEye[2];
+            viewAt.x = viewEye.x + (gSohVRCamFwd[0] * 100.0f);
+            viewAt.y = viewEye.y + (gSohVRCamFwd[1] * 100.0f);
+            viewAt.z = viewEye.z + (gSohVRCamFwd[2] * 100.0f);
+            viewUp.x = gSohVRCamUp[0];
+            viewUp.y = gSohVRCamUp[1];
+            viewUp.z = gSohVRCamUp[2];
+            viewFov = gSohVRCamFovy;
+            /* no zoom: the Hyrule Field 0.79 scale above would crop the
+             * deliberately-padded culling frustum. */
+            View_SetScale(&camera->play->view, 1.0f);
+        }
     }
+#endif
     camera->play->view.fovy = viewFov;
     func_800AA358(&camera->play->view, &viewEye, &viewAt, &viewUp);
     camera->camDir.x = eyeAtAngle.pitch;
